R-AL4 R-DI8 R-EF1 R-EF2 R-P5 R-UP7 R-EC12 R-DI9 R-CV1 R-DI12 (slice 068b, `PickLoop.probe_round!`, `PairOrder`): the hints order a round that the budget cuts. 1 run of `upgrade` with `[resolution] probe = { max = 2 }` and the world of `upgrade/ug2-lag` (a copy of its fixtures, the project q1h is q1 with the budget). No fact is in the db, so the loop asks for the unit checks of 4 pairs on the held compiler, in the order of the solver (slot order): json 2.2.0, text 2.0.0, parser 1.1.0, pfx 0.1.1. The budget has room for 2.
The round is cut (R-P5), so the order decides which 2 pairs run (R-AL4: "installed nightly first, then the strongest hint"). Only now the loop asks for hints (R-DI8: "only when the solver needs a hint for that candidate"): a round that the budget does not cut makes no hint call (the other cases of the suite are the proof: no `.roc-version` call in their `calls.log`). One `Github.hint!` for each release, in the order of the pairs:
json 2.2.0: no cache file, one request of the raw URL (no token), the fake answer is 404 (no route): the empty file is written, no hint. text 2.0.0 and pfx 0.1.1: the cache file `talon/index/github/acme/<repo>/<tag>.roc-version` is in `given/home` and names the held compiler: no request, the hint is rank 4 `pass` for that compiler. parser 1.1.0: no cache file, the request gets 500 (`fx/http/raw.githubusercontent.com/.../.roc-version.meta`): the answer is not kept (no write) and the failure is no hint (slice 068b D3: a hint only orders the search, R-EF2, so a failed request does not stop the command).
The pairs with a hint come first: text 2.0.0 and pfx 0.1.1 run (`probes 2`), json 2.2.0 and parser 1.1.0 do not. The run ends with exit 12 and `2 unit checks did not run` (R-UP7, R-EC12). Without the hint order the probes would be json and text.
Run 2 (`upgrade --offline`, q1o: the same project with `probe.max = 1`, after run 1, so the home has the cached index pages, the 2 facts of run 1 and the hint files of run 1): the 2 pairs that are left (json 2.2.0, parser 1.1.0) are cut to 1. `--offline` makes no request (R-DI8, R-DI12): the file of json 2.2.0 (empty: a 404 of run 1) is read and gives no hint, parser 1.1.0 has no file (run 1 did not keep the 500), so it has no hint and no request is made. No hint: the order of the solver, json is probed, exit 12 with `1 unit check did not run`. The line `index: cached at <time>` comes from `fx/mtimes` (R-DI12).
